**Exposure**
- `limited_exposure_with_choices`: Erdoğan had broad executive authority over national security, treaties, military deployment, and senior appointments, but Turkey had no independent nuclear arsenal. NATO’s forward-deployed weapons in Europe stayed under US custody and NATO political control.

**Reused Evidence**
- None beyond the local structured prior.

**New Evidence**
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Anayasa | Anayasa Mahkemesi","publisher":"Anayasa Mahkemesi","publication_date":"2017-01-21","url":"https://anayasa.gov.tr/tr/mevzuat/anayasa/","claim":"Article 104 vests executive authority in the President, including national-security policy, treaty ratification, appointment and dismissal of ministers and senior officials, military-use decisions, and presidential decrees subject to legal limits; Article 116 lets the TBMM or the President renew elections; Article 105 sets a parliamentary investigation path.","locator":"L1052-L1082, L1092-L1097, L1176-L1184","source_type":"official/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary constitutional text governing the 2022 presidency; direct and stable legal authority/constraint source.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Stable 2022 constitutional framework.","ruler_attribution":"Defines Erdoğan's office-level authority and checks in 2022; not a claim about personal conduct.","contrary_evidence":["The same articles constrain decree power and preserve parliamentary/judicial checks.","Formal authority does not prove how he used it in practice."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.5","1B.8","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"NATO’s nuclear deterrence policy and forces","publisher":"NATO","publication_date":"2026-05-20","url":"https://www.nato.int/en/what-we-do/deterrence-and-defence/natos-nuclear-deterrence-policy-and-forces","claim":"NATO says the United States maintains absolute control and custody of forward-deployed nuclear weapons in Europe, while Allies retain political control of nuclear deterrence and NATO remains committed to arms control, disarmament, and non-proliferation.","locator":"L813-L819, L836-L838","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Current NATO topic page directly states custody, control, and the alliance's nuclear policy framework.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Stable alliance structure relevant to 2022 and beyond.","ruler_attribution":"Shows Erdoğan did not control nuclear weapons independently; any role was alliance-level and indirect.","contrary_evidence":["This does not prove Turkey lacked all influence inside NATO consultations.","The page is current, so the wording is not a 2022 snapshot."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.6","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nuclear Planning Group (NPG)","publisher":"NATO","publication_date":"2026-05-20","url":"https://www.nato.int/en/about-us/organization/nato-structure/nuclear-planning-group-npg","claim":"The NPG is NATO's senior nuclear consultation body, covering policy, doctrine, planning, force posture, capabilities, exercises, and safety/security; all Allies except France are members, and decisions are by consensus.","locator":"L805-L809, L814-L814","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary NATO governance page describing nuclear decision structure and consultation rules.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Stable institutional context for 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Turkey, as a NATO Ally, participated in consultation rather than unilateral nuclear command.","contrary_evidence":["Membership does not equal unilateral control.","Consensus governance can diffuse responsibility."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.7"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Status of Signatures and Ratifications","publisher":"CTBTO","publication_date":"2026-07-14","url":"https://www.ctbto.org/our-mission/states-signatories","claim":"Türkiye signed the Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty on 24 September 1996 and ratified it on 16 February 2000; the treaty is still not in force.","locator":"Türkiye row, lines 769-771","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Treaty-status table from the CTBTO is the authoritative status source.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Valid status for 2022 and current comparison.","ruler_attribution":"Shows a formal non-testing, nonproliferation commitment inherited and maintained in Erdoğan's era, not a personal achievement by itself.","contrary_evidence":["CTBT ratification does not itself prove day-to-day restraint or crisis prudence.","The treaty is not yet in force, so legal effect is limited."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.6","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Country List: Türkiye, Republic of","publisher":"IAEA Office of Legal Affairs","publication_date":"2026-03-23","url":"https://ola.iaea.org/Applications/FactSheets/Country/Detail?code=TR","claim":"Türkiye has an NPT safeguards agreement in force and an Additional Protocol in force with the IAEA, which strengthens verification over declared nuclear material and activities.","locator":"L112-L124","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IAEA country fact sheet listing treaty and safeguards status.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Valid for 2022 and current status context.","ruler_attribution":"Supports the view that Turkey's nuclear posture is embedded in international verification, not unilateral national weapon control.","contrary_evidence":["Safeguards are about peaceful-use verification, not a blanket guarantee of prudent state behavior.","The page does not say anything about Erdoğan personally."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.6","1B.7","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Upgrades At US Nuclear Bases In Europe Acknowledge Security Risk","publisher":"Federation of American Scientists","publication_date":"2015-09-10","url":"https://fas.org/publication/nuclear-insecurity/","claim":"Incirlik Air Base in Turkey was described as the largest nuclear weapons storage site in Europe, located close to war-torn Syria, with security upgrades underway because of longstanding security concerns.","locator":"L49-L59, L63-L66","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_low","source_confidence_reason":"Technical open-source analysis from a specialist organization, but adversarial and partly inferential.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited-baseline context rather than 2022 conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Helps separate the inherited NATO storage posture from Erdoğan's personal choices.","contrary_evidence":["The piece is older than 2022 and partly normative.","It describes US/NATO storage arrangements more than Turkish decision-making."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Black Sea Grain Initiative Frequently Asked Questions","publisher":"United Nations in Türkiye","publication_date":"2022-08-18","url":"https://turkiye.un.org/en/195522-black-sea-grain-initiative-frequently-asked-questions","claim":"The Black Sea Grain Initiative was intended to reduce global hunger and food insecurity and ensure safe shipment of grain and foodstuffs, with a Joint Coordination Centre established in Istanbul and staffed by Türkiye, Russia, Ukraine, and the UN.","locator":"L61-L63","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN explanatory page on the initiative's purpose and structure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly about 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This is a positive, ruler-attributed de-escalation and humanitarian risk-reduction episode involving Erdoğan's government.","contrary_evidence":["It addresses food-security risk more than nuclear risk.","It does not by itself establish a broader nonproliferation record."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Coordination Centre opens in Istanbul to facilitate safe export of commercial foodstuffs and fertilizers from Ukrainian ports","publisher":"United Nations in Türkiye","publication_date":"2022-07-28","url":"https://turkiye.un.org/en/192332-joint-coordination-centre-opens-istanbul-facilitate-safe-export-commercial-foodstuffs-and","claim":"The UN said the JCC's swift opening was made possible with the invaluable support from Türkiye, and that the center would operationalize a humanitarian maritime corridor for safe exports from Ukraine.","locator":"L56-L61","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct UN press release describing Turkey's enabling role in the corridor implementation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous with the 2022 event.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly supports attribution to Erdoğan's government as host and facilitator, though implementation was multilateral.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian mediation does not equal arms-control leadership.","The claim concerns logistics and safety, not nuclear policy."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Türkiye, Finland, and Sweden sign agreement paving the way for Finnish and Swedish NATO membership","publisher":"NATO","publication_date":"2022-06-28","url":"https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/articles/news/2022/06/28/turkiye-finland-and-sweden-sign-agreement-paving-the-way-for-finnish-and-swedish-nato-membership","claim":"Erdoğan, Niinistö, and Andersson agreed a trilateral memorandum to address Türkiye's legitimate security concerns, paving the way for Finland and Sweden's NATO membership.","locator":"L813-L815","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary NATO summit statement on the agreement and its security rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Shows Erdoğan used alliance leverage in a negotiated setting rather than nuclear brinkmanship.","contrary_evidence":["This is alliance bargaining, not direct nuclear-risk reduction.","Turkey had a blocking position, so the move also reflected coercive leverage."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Cumhurbaşkanı Erdoğan: İsveç ve Finlandiya, Türkiye'nin güvenlik endişelerini dikkate almak zorunda","publisher":"Anadolu Ajansı","publication_date":"2022-06-28","url":"https://www.aa.com.tr/tr/gundem/cumhurbaskani-erdogan-isvec-ve-finlandiya-turkiyenin-guvenlik-endiselerini-dikkate-almak-zorunda/2624275","claim":"Erdoğan publicly said Sweden and Finland had to take Türkiye's security concerns into account if they were to join NATO.","locator":"L72-L73, L97-L100","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Major Turkish wire service with direct local-language reporting of Erdoğan's own statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous to the June 2022 NATO episode.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Erdoğan quotation, useful for attributing the bargaining posture to him personally.","contrary_evidence":["AA is state-aligned and may present the episode favorably to Ankara.","The quote is about security bargaining, not nuclear restraint."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Turkish air strikes target Kurdish militants in Syria, Iraq after bomb attack","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-21","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/21/syria-security-turkey","claim":"Turkish warplanes struck Kurdish militant bases in Syria and Iraq, destroying 89 targets, in retaliation for the Istanbul bombing.","locator":"L660-L668","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters dispatch reproduced by Euronews with a precise date and event details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Erdoğan's government and security posture, though the immediate operational order came through the defense ministry.","contrary_evidence":["Ankara framed the strikes as counterterrorism and retaliation.","This is conventional escalation, not nuclear escalation."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.8","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Erdogan says Turkey will launch Syria land operation when convenient","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-24","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/24/syria-security-turkey","claim":"Erdoğan said Turkey's air operations in northern Syria were only the beginning and that a land operation would be launched when convenient.","locator":"L643-L657","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters dispatch reproduced by Euronews, giving a direct quote from Erdoğan and the date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Erdoğan statement, relevant as a ruler-attributed escalation signal.","contrary_evidence":["The stated rationale was border security and counterterrorism.","It still reflects escalation risk, not de-escalation."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.5","1B.8","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Strategic Concepts","publisher":"NATO","publication_date":"2022-07-18","url":"https://www.nato.int/en/about-us/official-texts-and-resources/strategic-concepts","claim":"The 2022 Strategic Concept says NATO faces a deteriorated security environment, identifies Russia as the most significant threat, and names the erosion of arms control, disarmament, and non-proliferation architectures as a challenge.","locator":"L817-L820, L947-L951","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary NATO strategic text and explanatory page for the 2022 security environment.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly about the 2022 security environment.","ruler_attribution":"Background context for Erdoğan's alliance environment rather than a Turkey-specific nuclear decision.","contrary_evidence":["It is alliance context, not a ruler-specific conduct record.","It does not show Erdoğan personally advancing disarmament."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.10"]}

**What this means for Chapter 1B**
- Erdoğan in 2022 had real security authority, but not autonomous nuclear command.
- The strongest positive evidence is indirect: alliance de-escalation through the Finland/Sweden memorandum and the Black Sea grain corridor.
- The strongest negative evidence is conventional escalation in Syria and explicit readiness to expand that campaign.
- On the nuclear-specific side, the record is mostly institutional and inherited: NATO custody/control rules, CTBT/NPT-linked safeguards, and the Incirlik storage posture. That gives material context, but not a strong personal nuclear-risk profile.

**Search And Rejection Summary**
- Considered roughly 25-40 documents across NATO, UN, IAEA, CTBTO, Turkish official/legal pages, AA, Reuters/Euronews reproductions, and FAS.
- Kept sources that added distinct value on one of four things: Erdoğan's formal authority, NATO nuclear governance, treaty/nonproliferation status, and 2022 crisis behavior.
- Rejected as duplicates or weak signal: generic NATO intro pages, generic Turkey background pages, repeated Reuters wire copies of the same event, broad domestic politics/economy pieces, and post-2022 retrospectives that did not materially change the 2022 evidence picture.
- Used older FAS material only for inherited nuclear-risk context, not as direct 2022 conduct evidence.

**Remaining Gaps**
- No direct 2022 evidence located of Erdoğan making nuclear-specific rhetoric, threats, or doctrinal changes.
- No evidence that Erdoğan personally changed NATO nuclear posture, because Turkey did not control the weapons and NATO keeps political control collectively.
- More archival Turkish-language reporting could still refine 1B.2 and 1B.3, but the expected gain is modest unless you want a deeper dossier on alliance consultation or Incirlik security history.

**Compact Event Map**
- June 28, 2022: Erdoğan signs the Türkiye-Finland-Sweden memorandum in Madrid.
- July 22-28, 2022: Turkey hosts and helps operationalize the Black Sea Grain Initiative and JCC in Istanbul.
- November 21-24, 2022: Turkey strikes Kurdish targets in Syria/Iraq and Erdoğan signals a possible ground operation.
